 "about_text": "La Loma Projects is a Los Angeles gallery founded in 2019 by Kirk Nelson, which began informally in his home near La Loma Road before expanding in 2021 into a more formal exhibition space on North Figueroa Street. The gallery has built long-term relationships with a roster of established and mid-career artists while continuing to introduce new voices. Its program favors idea-driven exhibitions exploring the relationship between objects and meaning alongside painterly, handmade work attentive to humor, domesticity, materiality, and the natural world. La Loma also maintains an appointment-only annex space in Pasadena and regularly presents artists at international art fairs.",
